HISTORY_VERSION 1.0.0

TYPE Foundation

STATUS APPROVED

DATE 2026-07-06

TITLE

pace create implemented: PACE can now generate a brand-new project from scratch.

WHY

The President asked to be notified once PACE was ready to use for a new
project, naming Plataforma de Mantenimiento as the reason. Per the
roadmap, that is step 8 (pace create), which requires a real create
mode in Project Creator — until now the engine only had init mode
(attaching .pace/ to a project that already exists elsewhere).

DECISION

Added create_project() to engines/project_creator.py: creates the
target directory (refuses if it exists and is non-empty), runs
`git init` inside it, writes a minimal README.md, then calls
init_instance() to attach a valid .pace/. Deliberately does not generate
any stack-specific scaffolding (no framework files, no package.json) —
that remains a separate, later templates/ capability, not part of this
minimal create mode.

Added `pace create <path> --name --slug --org-ref` to cli/pace.py,
mirroring pace init's structure (reports the result, runs
validate_instance, warns if not clean).

Verified with 2 new engine tests (fresh project has .git/, README.md,
and a structurally valid .pace/; refuses a non-empty existing directory)
and 1 new CLI end-to-end test (create then doctor on a real temp path),
plus a manual run against a real temporary directory outside any test
fixture, confirming clean doctor/context output.

Test count: kernel 6, contract loader 4, project creator 8, CLI 4 — 22
total, all passing before this commit.

IMPACT

PACE can now originate a governed project from nothing, not just adopt
an existing one. This is what step 9 (creating Plataforma de
Mantenimiento) will use once the President is ready to run it for real.

NEXT_STEPS

Per the roadmap: adopt TuPeríMetro as the first governed *existing*
project (step 7, via pace init, still not done), and/or create
Plataforma de Mantenimiento as the first new project born from PACE
(step 9, via pace create, now ready) — order between these two is the
President's call, not fixed by dependency.

APPROVED_BY

President Cley Duarte

END
